From 501b7692084276364a9665b430241f31728c8ae2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mlmarcus <89200427+mlmarcus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:09:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(framegen): AMD FSR frame generation through the AMD FSR
 SDK 2.4 runtime

ASTROHYBRID_FSRFG=1 turns on AMD FSR frame generation (one generated frame per rendered frame) on any
Vulkan GPU with three spare queues in its graphics family (renderer/fsr.cpp, fsr.h). Kyty's swapchain
is created through FSR's frame-interpolation swapchain (acquire/present through its replacement
functions, the presented image left in SHADER_READ_ONLY_OPTIMAL); the frame hooks are DLSS-G's
(frameGen.cpp forwards them when FSR FG is requested): the camera from the game's per-view constants,
and at the temporal upscale pass copies of depth (R32F) and motion vectors into a small ring sized for
the largest render size seen. Prepare (PrepareV2) and the interpolation are recorded in the swapchain's
frame generation callback on the present thread; a frame without inputs shows the real frame twice.

Runtime: the SDK's signed amd_fidelityfx_loader_vk.dll (the one FSR upscaling, fsr.inc, already loads)
and amd_fidelityfx_framegeneration_vk.dll next to it, from ASTROHYBRID_FSR_PATH or the folder of
kyty_gpu.dll; headers only at build time (KYTY_FFX_SDK_DIR, framegeneration/include added). The
version structures SDK 2.1+ requires are chained; teardown follows the SDK 2.4 order (frame generation
configured off, its context destroyed, the swapchain context destroyed, then the swapchain handle
through pOutDestroySwapchainFFXAPI). The device-proc-address callback falls back to the core name
for *KHR functions Kyty's device has as core Vulkan 1.1+ (the backend asked for
vkGetBufferMemoryRequirements2KHR unchecked and crashed on the first run).

It works with the game's own upscaling, DLSS and FSR upscaling; DLSS-G (ASTROHYBRID_DLSSG) wins when
both are requested, and VK_NV_low_latency2 stays off with it. While it is on the image cache budget
leaves 1 GiB more video memory free (vma.cpp). One "FSR FG 10s:" line every 10 s ends with the video
memory in use. Options: ASTROHYBRID_FSRFG_ASYNC=0, ASTROHYBRID_FSRFG_DEBUG=1, ASTROHYBRID_FSRFG_HUD=0
(a HUD-less copy of the display buffer; its capture point does not trigger in Astro Bot yet).

